  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 218 PM EST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nDry and Warming Up Into Next Weekend:\n\nFrom the early to middle portions of the upcoming week, the longwave \ntrough that provided a chilly weekend will finally get kicked off to \nthe northeast as a shortwave slides from the Southern Plains into \nthe eastern Gulf. This wave will not have much moisture or punch to \nit as it slides through our area, and has actually trended further \nsouth in its track, bringing rain chances down to under 10% across \nCentral GA. The cool airmass from the weekend will be shoved out, \nallowing highs to gradually climb back into the 60s by Wednesday, \nwith overnight lows returning to above freezing. Behind this system, \na ridge will build from the Gulf up across the Southeast US during \nthe second half of the week and into next weekend. Our stretch of \ndry weather will continue in this setup, and temperatures will warm \nup to around 10F above normal. Highs will climb back into the 70s \nby Friday, with overnight lows in the 40s to near 50.",
